fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A1
# @code: A1
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A1: Euler–Bernoulli & Timoshenko Cantilever Tip Deflection & Root Stress (V1 / V2)
# @subtitle: Verify Fieldsmith’s 10-node quadratic (P2) tetrahedral elasticity solver against closed-form Euler–Bernoulli and Timoshenko beam theory on a 100 × 10 × 10 mm steel cantilever under a 100 N tip shear load.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V1 & V2 · Closed-Form Beam Theory · PASS (< 1.5%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A1-cantilever-beam-theory.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A1-cantilever-beam-theory.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a1-euler-bernoulli-cantilever.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V1.md, docs/verification/V2.md
# ---
# @check: Tip Vertical Deflection u_z(L) || δ_EB = F L³ / (3 E I) = 0.2000 mm;  δ_Timo = δ_EB + F L / (κ A G) = 0.2016 mm || 0.2016 mm || 0.1994 mm || 1.09% || ≤ 2.0%
# @check: Mid-Span Fiber Bending Stress σ_xx(x=50 mm, z=10 mm) || σ_xx(x, z) = M(x) · (z - z₀) / I = F (L - x) c / I || 30.00 MPa || 29.96 MPa || 0.13% || ≤ 1.5%
# @check: External Work Compliance C = fᵀ u || C_Timo = F · δ_Timo = 20.156 N·mm (Galerkin lower bound C_h ≤ C_exact) || 20.156 N·mm || 19.940 N·mm || 1.07% || ≤ 2.0%
# ---
# @assert: Timoshenko Tip Deflection δ_tip || max_displacement || 0.2016 || 2.5% || mm
# @assert: External Work Compliance C = fᵀ u || compliance || 20.156 || 2.5% || N·mm
# @assert: Tip Shear Resultant |R| || resultant_mag || 100.0 || 0.5% || N
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect the Canonical 100 × 10 × 10 mm Cantilever Geometry & Boundary Conditions || setup
#   Open Setup (2). The beam has length L = 100 mm along X and a square b × h = 10 × 10 mm cross-section (area A = 100 mm², second moment of area I = b h³ / 12 = 833.333 mm⁴) with Young’s modulus E = 200,000 MPa and Poisson’s ratio ν = 0.30. The root face x = 0 ("root") is clamped (fixed=xyz) and the free tip x = 100 mm ("tip") carries a downward shear force F = 100 N.
# @expected:
#   Setup highlights the x = 0 root clamp and the −100 N Z-load distributed over the 10 × 10 mm tip face.
# @step: 2. Verify Tip Deflection & Mid-Span Bending Stress Against Closed-Form Beam Theory || results
#   Switch to Results (3). By Euler–Bernoulli theory, tip deflection is δ_EB = F L³ / (3 E I) = 100 × 10⁶ / (3 × 200,000 × 833.333) = 0.2000 mm; adding Cowper’s transverse shear deflection δ_shear = F L / (κ A G) with κ = 5/6 and G = 76,923 MPa gives δ_Timo = 0.2016 mm. At mid-span (x = 50 mm, away from the 3D Poisson root clamp), outer-fiber bending stress is σ_xx = F (L − x) (h/2) / I = 100 × 50 × 5 / 833.333 = 30.00 MPa.
# @expected:
#   Fieldsmith P2 FEA reproduces mid-span fiber stress within 0.15% and tip deflection within 1.1% of the closed-form Timoshenko reference.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A1 — Euler–Bernoulli & Timoshenko Cantilever Flexure (V1 / V2)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the exact 1D Euler–Bernoulli and Timoshenko cantilever deflection and bending stress formulas and explains why 10-node quadratic (P2) tetrahedra avoid the shear locking of 4-node linear (P1) elements.
# @theory_section: A1.1 Closed-Form Flexural & Transverse Shear Deflection
# @theory_eq:
#   I = b h³ / 12 = 833.333 mm⁴,     G = E / (2(1 + ν)) = 76,923.1 MPa
#   δ_total = F L³ / (3 E I) + F L / (κ A G) = 0.20000 + 0.00156 = 0.20156 mm
#   σ_xx(x, z) = F (L − x) (z − h/2) / I
# @theory_body:
#   Because the P2 basis contains complete degree-2 polynomials on each tetrahedron, the linear bending strain ε_xx(z) ∝ (z − h/2) lies inside the finite-element approximation space, eliminating P1 shear locking.
# ---
# @mcp: Run Cantilever Solve via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":30000}
#   Solve the V1/V2 cantilever benchmark and return peak deflection and compliance.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A1 — Euler-Bernoulli Cantilever Benchmark (V1/V2)"
custommaterial steel200 name="Steel (E=200 GPa, nu=0.30)" e=200000 nu=0.30 yield=250 density=7.85
material steel200

box beam size=(100, 10, 10) at=(50, 5, 5)
region root = beam.nx
region tip = beam.px
support clamp root fixed=xyz
load shear tip force=(0, 0, -100)
solve
